{"header":{"status":{"name":"Success","code":0,"description":"Query success","apiHelp":"https://www.censtatd.gov.hk/en/web_table.html?id=340-45012&api_popup=1"},"title":"Money supply (Hong Kong dollar and foreign currency)","tablenote":["Figures are as at end of the period.     Figures refer to all authorized institutions (AIs), which include licensed banks, restricted licence banks (RLBs) and deposit-taking companies (DTCs).     Figures are revised on a monthly basis to take into account any subsequent amendments submitted by AIs.     RLBs can accept time deposits in amounts of not less than HK$500,000 with any term of maturity. There is no restriction on interest rate payable.     DTCs can accept time deposits in amounts of not less than HK$100,000 with a term of maturity of at least 3 months. There is no restriction on interest rate payable.     Among the various monetary aggregates, seasonal patterns are found in Hong Kong dollar (HKD) M1, currency held by the public, and demand deposits. Seasonally adjusted data on the three series facilitate the analysis of underlying trends.     Foreign currency swap deposits are deposits involving customers buying foreign currencies in the spot market and placing them as deposits with authorized institutions, while at the same time entering into a forward contract to sell such foreign currencies (principal plus interest) upon maturity of such deposits. For most analytical purposes, these should be regarded as Hong Kong dollar deposits.","Money supply M1 refers to the sum of legal tender notes and coins held by the public plus customers' demand deposits placed with licensed banks.","Money supply M2 refers to the sum of M1 plus customers' savings and time deposits with licensed banks, plus negotiable certificates of deposits (NCDs) issued by licensed banks held by non-AIs.","Money supply M3 refers to the sum of M2 plus customer deposits with RLBs and DTCs plus NCDs issued by RLBs and DTCs held by non-AIs."],"source":"Hong Kong Monetary Authority For further information, please visit the website of the Hong Kong Monetary Authority (www.hkma.gov.hk/eng) (Enquiry telephone no. : 2878 8222  Enquiry e-mail : hkma@hkma.gov.hk)","count":{"noOfRecords":64}},"dataSet":[{"CURRENCY":"","CURRENCYDesc":"Total","freq":"Y","period":"1997","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":208093,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":1,"CURRENCYDesc":"HK dollar","freq":"Y","period":"1997","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":188135,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":3,"CURRENCYDesc":"Foreign currency","freq":"Y","period":"1997","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":19958,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":"","CURRENCYDesc":"Total","freq":"Q","period":"199706","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":226855,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":1,"CURRENCYDesc":"HK dollar","freq":"Q","period":"199706","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":204922,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":3,"CURRENCYDesc":"Foreign currency","freq":"Q","period":"199706","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":21933,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":"","CURRENCYDesc":"Total","freq":"Y","period":"2025","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":3109917,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":1,"CURRENCYDesc":"HK dollar","freq":"Y","period":"2025","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":1734389,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":3,"CURRENCYDesc":"Foreign currency","freq":"Y","period":"2025","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":1375528,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":"","CURRENCYDesc":"Total","freq":"Q","period":"202606","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":3481515,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":1,"CURRENCYDesc":"HK dollar","freq":"Q","period":"202606","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":1835077,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":3,"CURRENCYDesc":"Foreign currency","freq":"Q","period":"202606","sv":"M1","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":1646437,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":"","CURRENCYDesc":"Total","freq":"Y","period":"1997","sv":"M2_SW","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":2788808,"sd_value":""},{"CURRENCY":